<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Kaulonia</h1><p class="st-meta">675 BCE – 389 BCE (approx.) · capital Kaulonia</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Achaean Greek city on the Calabrian coast, a dependency of Croton, destroyed by Dionysius I of Syracuse in 389 BCE.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Kaulonia was founded in the 7th century BCE on the Ionian coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/calabria">Calabria</a>, near modern Monasterace Marina, by Achaean settlers, probably sent out by <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/croton">Croton</a>, to secure its southern border against <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/locri-epizephyrii">Locri</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Kaulonia remained closely tied to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/croton">Croton</a>. Its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> coins, showing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apollo">Apollo</a> carrying a small running figure and a deer, are among the finest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magna-graecia">Magna Graecia</a>. Excavations have uncovered a Doric temple, walls and houses, and a large floor mosaic with a dragon of the 3rd century BCE. Little is known of its government.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After defeating the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/italiote-league">Italiote League</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-elleporus">Elleporus</a> river in 389 BCE, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dionysius-i-of-syracuse">Dionysius I</a> took Kaulonia, moved its people to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/syracuse">Syracuse</a> and gave its land to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/locri-epizephyrii">Locri</a>. A smaller town revived later but was destroyed during the wars with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyrrhus-of-epirus">Pyrrhus</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hannibal">Hannibal</a>, and by the Roman period the site was deserted.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kaulonia.jpg" alt="Kaulonia" width="320" height="240"><figcaption>Image: Marcuscalabresus · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kaulon_2009_tempio.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>675 BCE – 389 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/7th-century-bce">7th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>city state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kaulonia</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Greek religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Achaean Greek</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Caulonia</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-532&amp;focus=kaulonia" aria-label="Kaulonia on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5092 797 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kaulonia lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5412 1053L5383 1099"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5383 1099h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5412 1053h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5412 1053h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=-532&amp;focus=kaulonia">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
